\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces (A) Interfacial-excess amplitude \(|\delta \phi _+| = |\phi _+(0) - \bar  \phi |\) for the numerical (dashed) and analytical (solid) results as a function of the chemical potential difference \(\mu _c-\mu \). The colorscale indicates the interaction strength \(\eta \) and \(\chi =2.5\). Note that the analytical solution always overestimates \(\delta \phi _+\). (B) Relative error \(\epsilon _{\mathrm  {approx.}}=|\delta \phi _+^{\mathrm  {analytical}} - \delta \phi _+^{\mathrm  {numerical}}| / |\delta \phi _+^{\mathrm  {numerical}}|\) of the analytical approximation. The analytical solution becomes exact near the critical point. Surprisingly, the relative error seems to vanish near the binary-mixture limit \((\phi _0 \to 0)\) as well, suggesting that the curvature can be neglected in this regime as well. \relax }}{34}{}\protected@file@percent }
